<title>CHILE: Chile's Enersis confirms Brazil Cerj win.</title>
<headline>Chile's Enersis confirms Brazil Cerj win.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean power investment company Enersis SA said a consortium including its Chilectra unit bought Wednesday a 70.2 percent stake in Brazilian power firm Cerj.</p>
<p>The Rio de Janeiro bourse said the group, which includes Spain's Endesa and Eletricidade de Portugal, won the auction with an offer of 605.3 million reais.</p>
<p>Enersis' chief executive Jose Yuraszeck will hold a news conference at 1600 local time/1900 GMT to discuss the purchase.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595 x212</p>
</text>
